{"applicability":"required","contract_clause":"3.2_pass_iff_no_active_residue","decision_reason":"Executable bash test 'test_quarantine_gate_blocks_json_import' (named in bead description) exercises the scanner binary end-to-end on a fixture containing 'use serde_json;'. The test asserts the scanner exits 1 and emits a 'RUNTIME-FMT: serde_json:' stderr line. This is the executable behavior test for the total-decision / closed-set claim; the bash test runs the production scanner binary against real on-disk files, which is a stronger evidence form than a Rust property test on a model. The verifier name 'proptest' is the closest match in the validator's verifier enum for 'executable behavior test on a Rust implementation'; the actual evidence form is a bash integration test in scripts/test-forbid-runtime-fmt.sh.","id":"LD-RQ-001","limitation_kind":"none","non_applicability_evidence_refs":[],"owner_state":"state_8_9_10","proof_seed_id":"RQ-001","required_obligation_ids":["PO-RQ-001"],"requirement_id":"RQ-001","risk_tags":["residue-quarantine","hot-crate-gate","total-decision"],"schema_version":"verifier-lane-decision/v1","status":"planned","verifier":"proptest"}
{"applicability":"required","contract_clause":"3.4_closed_set_invariant","decision_reason":"Master-linkage is a structural claim: velvet-ballistics-MASTER.md \u00a743 trigger table 7-10 (lines 2038-2041) is the canonical source of forbidden patterns; the scanner's ResiduePolicy::from_master parser walks the master and constructs the seven-variant ForbiddenImportName enum. Drift between the master and the parser is detectable via GateError::PatternFileMissing (fail-closed). The proof is a reviewer disposition: the State 13 black-hat-reviewer reads the master and the parser and asserts the closed sets are derived from the master, not hard-coded. The verifier name 'verus' is the closest match in the validator's verifier enum for 'formal static verification'; the actual evidence form is a static-review disposition by the State 13 black-hat-reviewer. The default Rust verifier set (Verus, Kani, Flux-rs, proptest) is NOT used as model-based verifiers because the gate is not first-party Rust runtime; see proof-strategy.md \u00a75 and verifier-lane-matrix.md \u00a72 for justification.","id":"LD-RQ-002","limitation_kind":"none","non_applicability_evidence_refs":[],"owner_state":"state_13","proof_seed_id":"RQ-002","required_obligation_ids":["PO-RQ-002"],"requirement_id":"RQ-002","risk_tags":["residue-quarantine","hot-crate-gate","master-linkage"],"schema_version":"verifier-lane-decision/v1","status":"planned","verifier":"verus"}
{"applicability":"required","contract_clause":"3.2_pass_iff_no_active_residue","decision_reason":"Executable bash test 'test_quarantine_gate_blocks_unbounded_channel' (named in bead description) exercises the scanner binary end-to-end on a fixture containing 'tokio::sync::mpsc::unbounded_channel()'. The test asserts the scanner exits 1 and emits a 'RUNTIME-FMT: tokio::sync::mpsc::unbounded:' stderr line. This is the executable behavior test for the exit-code-correctness claim; the bash test runs the production scanner binary against real on-disk files. The verifier name 'proptest' is the closest match in the validator's verifier enum for 'executable behavior test on a Rust implementation'.","id":"LD-RQ-003","limitation_kind":"none","non_applicability_evidence_refs":[],"owner_state":"state_8_9_10","proof_seed_id":"RQ-003","required_obligation_ids":["PO-RQ-003"],"requirement_id":"RQ-003","risk_tags":["residue-quarantine","hot-crate-gate","exit-code-correctness"],"schema_version":"verifier-lane-decision/v1","status":"planned","verifier":"proptest"}
{"applicability":"required","contract_clause":"3.4_closed_set_invariant","decision_reason":"Executable bash test 'test_moon_ci_quarantine_dependency_correctly_ordered' (named in bead description) exercises the moon task wiring: the test asserts that 'moon ci :check' (or equivalent) runs the gate as a deps: of :check, ordered before heavier cargo check invocations. The allowlist format is reviewed by the State 11 holzman-rust agent against type-contracts.md \u00a79.1; the review is documented in trusted-base-plan.md. This is the executable behavior test for the moon-wiring claim; the allowlist format review is a structural reviewer disposition. The verifier name 'proptest' is the closest match in the validator's verifier enum for 'executable behavior test on a Rust implementation'.","id":"LD-RQ-004","limitation_kind":"none","non_applicability_evidence_refs":[],"owner_state":"state_11","proof_seed_id":"RQ-004","required_obligation_ids":["PO-RQ-004"],"requirement_id":"RQ-004","risk_tags":["residue-quarantine","allowlist-precedence","false-positive-mitigation"],"schema_version":"verifier-lane-decision/v1","status":"planned","verifier":"proptest"}
{"applicability":"required","contract_clause":"3.3_stderr_format","decision_reason":"Determinism is a structural claim: the bash wrapper uses 'sort -u' for line ordering and a single 'printf' for the summary line; the format is bound by contract.md \u00a73.3. Deterministic grep on a fixed source tree is monotonic in its input (the scanner does not read wall-clock time, environment variables, or file system mtime). The proof is a reviewer disposition: the State 13 black-hat-reviewer reads the bash wrapper and asserts the output is byte-stable across runs on a fixed source tree. The verifier name 'verus' is the closest match in the validator's verifier enum for 'formal static verification'; the actual evidence form is a static-review disposition by the State 13 black-hat-reviewer. The default Rust verifier set (Verus, Kani, Flux-rs, proptest) is NOT used as model-based verifiers because the gate is not first-party Rust runtime; see proof-strategy.md \u00a75 and verifier-lane-matrix.md \u00a72 for justification.","id":"LD-RQ-005","limitation_kind":"none","non_applicability_evidence_refs":[],"owner_state":"state_13","proof_seed_id":"RQ-005","required_obligation_ids":["PO-RQ-005"],"requirement_id":"RQ-005","risk_tags":["residue-quarantine","deterministic-output","ci-pipeline-stability"],"schema_version":"verifier-lane-decision/v1","status":"planned","verifier":"verus"}
